    "text": "To determine how many more apple pies Steve bakes than cherry pies in one week, we need to follow these steps:\n\n1. Calculate the total number of apple pies baked in one week.\n2. Calculate the total number of cherry pies baked in one week.\n3. Find the difference between the number of apple pies and cherry pies.\n\nFirst, let's calculate the total number of apple pies baked in one week. Steve bakes apple pies on Mondays, Wednesdays, and Fridays. There are 3 days in these weeks, and he bakes 12 pies each day. So, the total number of apple pies is:\n\\[ 3 \\text{ days} \\times 12 \\text{ pies/day} = 36 \\text{ apple pies} \\]\n\nNext, let's calculate the total number of cherry pies baked in one week. Steve bakes cherry pies on Tuesdays and Thursdays. There are 2 days in these weeks, and he bakes 12 pies each day. So, the total number of cherry pies is:\n\\[ 2 \\text{ days} \\times 12 \\text{ pies/day} = 24 \\text{ cherry pies} \\]\n\nNow, we find the difference between the number of apple pies and cherry pies:\n\\[ 36 \\text{ apple pies} - 24 \\text{ cherry pies} = 12 \\text{ more apple pies} \\]\n\nTherefore, the number of more apple pies Steve bakes than cherry pies in one week is \\(\\boxed{12}\\).",
